# A. AGENT DISCOVERY / SEO / DISTRIBUTION

## 1. AgentRank — empirical SEO for agents

**Priority: P0**

### Problem

Existing GEO/AEO products mostly monitor mentions and citations. Several current products already cover ChatGPT/Perplexity/Gemini visibility, and open-source tools can already run basic AI-visibility audits. ([NBound Marketing][4])

The harder problem is:

> **What actually causes an agent to retrieve, trust, cite, absorb and act on a source?**

### Architecture

```text
Query Corpus
    ↓
query paraphrase generator
    ↓
┌ ChatGPT/Search
├ Gemini
├ Perplexity
├ Claude/search
└ other engines
    ↓
retrieval/citation capture
    ↓
CitationEvent
    ↓
page fetch + feature extraction
    ↓
72+ page/domain/protocol features
    ↓
multivariate attribution
    ↓
controlled site experiments
    ↓
repeat queries
    ↓
causal-ish delta estimator
```

Features:

```text
domain
TLD
domain age
source class
earned/owned/community
page age
freshness
semantic HTML
heading density
JSON-LD
citations
numerical evidence
tables
definitions
page length
token count
latency
SSR/static/client-rendered
robots policy
OAI-SearchBot accessibility
llms.txt
agents.txt
OpenAPI
MCP
canonical
sitemap
language
location
```

### Important principle

Do **not** declare:

```text
.ts > .js
Astro > Next
.com > .ai
```

from intuition.

Build equivalent controlled sites and actually test them.

Agents primarily see the resulting HTTP/content surface, so implementation language should be treated as an experimental variable only where it changes rendering, latency, availability or structure.

### Internal value

Automatically optimize:

* GitGoblin
* AlternativeAPI
* Egoic
* QDW
* every generated product.

### Public product

```text
agentrank.com/{domain}

POST /experiments
GET /visibility
GET /citations
GET /source-preference
GET /recommendations
```

### Moat

Longitudinal black-box measurements of how actual engines behave.

