# Shared repo strategy

The products should **look independent externally**, while internally importing a small stable common library.

Not:

```text
gigantic monorepo
where everything knows everything
```

Prefer:

```text
qdw-contracts
qdw-evidence
qdw-provenance
qdw-client
```

plus independent repositories:

```text
agentrank/
agentreach/
toolpulse/
painfinder/
stackoracle/
alternativeapi/
...
```

Their integration boundary is JSON/HTTP/events, not Python imports across every repository.

Example:

```text
ToolPulse
    │
    ├── POST WorldState Observation
    │
    └── emits capability.health.changed

StackOracle
    │
    └── consumes capability.health.changed

ToolRouter
    │
    └── queries StackOracle

Cuntgoblin
    │
    └── queries ToolRouter
```

This preserves the ability to:

* sell a product separately;
* open-source one product;
* replace implementation languages;
* deploy independently;
* keep the shared intelligence core private.

