# One particularly important architectural decision

There are really **three classes** in the 50:

### Sensors

Observe reality.

```text
GitGoblin
Painfinder
ToolPulse
AgentRank
FundingRadar
PolicyPulse
WebChange
```

### Oracles

Turn observations into decisions.

```text
StackOracle
AlternativeAPI
ToolRouter
DistributionOracle
OpportunityGraph
```

### Actuators/factories

Change reality.

```text
AgentReady Compiler
AgentReach
Cuntgoblin
Factory system
distribution/publishing
```

QDW sits across all three and asks:

```text
What was observed?
What was inferred?
What was actually done?
How do we prove each?
```

That separation is what prevents the ecosystem becoming an enormous self-referential pile of agents confidently telling one another that they succeeded.

